> won't break more plugins than solution without the interface

Just looked at the previous commit. Okay, as you said, the previous commit also broke existing preemption plugins as much as the current version with `Reader` interface too.

Then, another angle though, how about just adding a status to PostFilter interface, rather than managing it in NodeToStatusMap in the first place? (or any reason you're trying to evolve NodeToStatusMap?)

```go
// ...
// filterStatus is a status aggregated from prefilter or filter plugins status.  
// If the pod was rejected completely at PreFilter phase, filterStatus would be the same status as the one returned from RunPreFilterPlugins.
// And, if the Pod was rejected at Filter phase, it'd be Unschedulable if any Node was rejected with Unschedulable, otherwise UnschedulableAndUnresolvable.
PostFilter(ctx context.Context, state *CycleState, pod *v1.Pod, filteredNodeStatusMap NodeToStatusMap, filterStatus *Status) (*PostFilterResult, *Status)
```

Then, preemption PostFilter plugins can just return early when filterStatus is UnschedulableAndUnresolvable.
Would this idea reduce a required change + eliminate all the change to NodeToStatusMap? 
We, either way, break-change PostFilter interface with a new param though, people can just ignore a new param if they don't need it.

